on getObjectsTableAddress (adrSite, flMessage=false) {
	«Get the address of the table of objects for this site. If it's a dg message, the checkouts table is in the discussion group. If it's an advanced item, the checkouts table is in the #newsSite table of the site.
		«02/08/00; 10:18:51 PM by PBS
		«Changes:
			«02/09/00; 7:11:49 PM by PBS
				«The checkouts table has been moved to the #newsSite table inside the site.
			«02/10/00; 11:38:55 AM by PBS
				«There are now two checkouts tables, one in the dg and one in the site itself. This is because Manila sites may share a dg, but having two sites shouldn't be a way to circumvent custody.
	
	local (adrCheckOuts);
	
	if flMessage { //the checkouts table is in the discussion group
		local (adrDg);
		local (dgName = adrSite^.["#prefs"].discussionRoot);
		manilaSuite.discuss.rpcGetGroupAddress (dgName, @adrDg);
		adrCheckouts = @adrDg^.checkouts;
		if not defined (adrCheckouts^) {
			new (tableType, adrCheckouts)}}
	else { //the checkouts table is in the site itself
		local (adrNewsSite = @adrSite^.["#newsSite"]);
		
		adrCheckouts = @adrNewsSite^.checkouts;
		if not defined (adrCheckouts^) {
			new (tableType, adrCheckouts)}};
	
	return (adrCheckouts)}